            <div xml:id="d1453">

                <pb facs="1558" n="1544" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.24/8–2444: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-02T14:10:00-04:00">September 2,
                            1944—2:10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–659. Your airgram No. A–817, August 24, noon. The considerations outlined in
                    the Department’s telegram no. 864 of August 17, 6 p.m. do not apply with regard
                    to purchases made by Peru in other <pb facs="1559" n="1545" xml:id="pg1545"/>
                    South American countries including Argentina, since there is no question of
                    violation of United States export controls.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
